<BlogPost
  title="Color-Drenching with Shiloh and Eclipse: The Custom Paint Ordering Guide"
  description="How to order any Sherwin-Williams color on Shiloh or Eclipse: the 20% Custom Paint upcharge plus species, the $750 list fee under $15,000, sample sizes and prices, the Eclipse edge-band step, the Custom Finish Approval Form, and how to set it up in 2020 Design Flex."
  author="Ben Miller"
  publishedDate="2026-07-31"
  ogImage="/images/blog/custom-paint-color-drenching/listing-card.webp"
  heroImage="/images/blog/custom-paint-color-drenching/sherwin-williams-fan-deck.webp"
>

<p><strong>Color-drenching</strong> — carrying one color across the walls, trim, and cabinetry of a room — only works if the cabinets can match the paint on the wall. That's exactly what the Custom Paint program does: <a href="/brands/eclipse-cabinetry/">Eclipse</a> and <a href="/brands/shiloh-cabinetry/">Shiloh</a> cabinets can be finished in <strong>almost any Sherwin-Williams paint color</strong>.</p>

<div class="post-figure">
  <img src="/images/blog/custom-paint-color-drenching/sherwin-williams-fan-deck.webp" alt="Sherwin-Williams color fan deck" width="738" height="414" fetchpriority="high" />
</div>

<h2>Pricing</h2>

<ul>
  <li><strong>Custom Paint finish: 20%</strong>, added to your species upcharge. Example: 20% Custom Paint + 8% Maple = <strong>28%</strong> added to the order list price.</li>
  <li><strong>Orders under $15,000 list</strong> are charged an additional <strong>$750 list</strong> custom paint fee.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Step 1: Identify the color early</h2>

<p>Get the Sherwin-Williams color number from the client <strong>as early as possible</strong> — the sample door has to be made and approved before the project order goes in.</p>

<h2>Step 2: Follow the steps for your line</h2>

<div class="steps-grid">
  <div class="steps-card">
    <h3>Eclipse</h3>
    <ol>
      <li><strong>Email <a href="mailto:customer.service@wwinc.com">customer.service@wwinc.com</a></strong> to confirm a matching <strong>edge-band for the box</strong> is available in that color. Reach out to your rep with questions.</li>
      <li>Order a sample: <strong>CM 8½ × 11</strong> ($350 list) or <strong>CM 12½ × 15½</strong> ($585 list).</li>
      <li>On the order, enter the Sherwin-Williams color code (e.g. <strong>SW6671</strong>) as the color on the Eclipse order form, or put it in special instructions.</li>
      <li>Fill out the <strong>Custom Finish Approval Form</strong> and submit it with your Standard Order.</li>
    </ol>
  </div>
  <div class="steps-card">
    <h3>Shiloh</h3>
    <ol>
      <li>Order a sample: <strong>CM 8½ × 11</strong> ($350 list) or <strong>CM 12½ × 15½</strong> ($585 list).</li>
      <li>On the order, enter the Sherwin-Williams color code (e.g. <strong>SW6671</strong>) as the color on the Shiloh order form, or put it in special instructions.</li>
      <li>Fill out the <strong>Custom Finish Approval Form</strong> and submit it with your Standard Order.</li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</div>

<p><strong>Lead time:</strong> as long as the sample door has been received <em>before</em> you submit the project order, Custom Paint adds <strong>no lead time</strong>.</p>

<h2>Step 3: Set it up in 2020 Design Flex</h2>

<ol>
  <li>In the Finishes step, select <strong>Custom Paint (Specify SW#)</strong>.</li>
  <li>Find the Sherwin-Williams color: in the Textures browser, open <strong>Catalog Textures → Paint → Sherwin Williams</strong> and pick the color by name and SW number.</li>
  <li>Change <strong>all</strong> variables to the custom color — door texture, drawer front, and both frame (horizontal and vertical) textures — so the rendering and the order match.</li>
  <li>If the order doesn't meet the <strong>$15,000 list</strong> minimum, add the custom paint upcharge item (<strong>CUSTPNT-UPCH</strong>, $750).</li>
</ol>

